WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.900
Claimant: Hi, I found my parked car with a scratched door and a broken side window the next morning. The repairs are estimated at $1,400.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.650
Adjuster: I'm sorry you found your car like that—do you know what caused the damage?

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.800
Claimant: I don’t know what caused it. I found the damage the next morning after the car was parked overnight.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:47.300
Adjuster: Decision: requires further review. The claimant reports a scratched door and broken side window, but does not know the cause; the policy covers vandalism and glass breakage other than from collision. Whether the damage resulted from a covered other-than-collision cause remains unresolved. Next action: Obtain a damage inspection and any available incident evidence to determine whether the door damage and glass breakage qualify as other-than-collision losses.
